			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3232">halose7n</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/13/2002 - 8:14 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2882">Serenna Nytefyrre</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2588">Laine L`ssinurn</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3170">Teriel L`ssinurn</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3103">Ellewinne</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3214">Rathil</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3213">Terial</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Soloing depends on class, level, and amount of twinkage, and generally amounts to yielding more XP, albiet less steadily and is more dangerous.<br />
<br />
Grouping doesn't have any dependancies, and it's a lot safer (in general), and the experience is steady.<br />
<br />
If you can solo, for your level range, it is generally more efficient to do than grouping, but there are some niceties to grouping, such as being able to work on different skills (for melees) without being in danger of dying or lots of downtime.<br />
<br />
Hope that's what you were looking for..						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3296">cherilyn</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/14/2002 - 3:43 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2719">Saddori Tonkatuff</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Chanters are the mob control in a WELL balanced group.  Generally this is the way to go.  Although it is highly advised that they continue to solo here and there...with the right combination of spells you and your pet can get a nice harmony going and build up skills you need to keep the group safe at higher levels.						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3232">halose7n</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/14/2002 - 7:49 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2882">Serenna Nytefyrre</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2588">Laine L`ssinurn</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3170">Teriel L`ssinurn</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3103">Ellewinne</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3214">Rathil</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3213">Terial</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														I'll also add some of my experiences playing varioius classes.<br />
<br />
Druids:  Soloing is viable most of until low-teens. Once you receive SoW at 14, and a DoT (19? I can't remember) you could continue, but it's best to group until 34, when you can quad-kite to solo. From there it's a matter of doing what you want; druids aren't group dependant afterwards.<br />
<br />
Monk: Easy to solo to 60, but it's hard on the skills, and boring after a while. Feign Death, and to a lesser extent, Mend, is what makes it possible. Serenna joined groups to work up her combat skills as they fell behind.<br />
<br />
Rogue: Soloable until late teens, then the need for groups is very apparent. Backstabbing requires someone to take aggro off of you, and it's the main way to do damage. Rogues do not have enough hit points to keep soloing.						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=2063">Aamain</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/14/2002 - 8:23 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=1578">Aamain Nobleshadow</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=1962">Aamaorn Nobleshadow</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2012">Aatun Nobleshadow</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2034">Alladric Nobleshadow</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2715">Aagein Nobleshadow</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3775">Sshaamy</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2855">Coffer</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3768">Aaliam</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=1989">Aadain</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2755">Aagain</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3189">Aaralron</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2757">Aaclef</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2758">Aamaine</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2759">Rubal</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2013">Vnayil</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3039">Aakitt</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														ok...getting warmer, each class can do both...some easier than others...I guess what I'm after here is in the roles for each class in a group, how do they interasct with each othe as opposed to handling themselves in a soloing role						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3291">Cuedyen</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/14/2002 - 1:47 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2645">Cuedyen Abuhannah</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2878">Legween Abuhannah</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Aamain,<br />
<br />
I play both my druid and paly solo and grouped (paly solo's still at 50).<br />
<br />
Druids use entirely different skill sets when they solo, be it quad kite or single kite.  When soloing, i keep offensive spells memmed, root, snare, and GHeal in case i oops.  At different levels DD or DoT will be more mana efficient depending on the spell set.  Basically, snare pull, root, dot x2 or snare nuke backup, nuke, backup, nuke....<br />
<br />
When grouped, i have almost 0 offensive spells since I am called on more to heal/sow/snare/DS/Regen/STR - rarely do i get to nuke :( <br />
<br />
Paly uses almost identical skills either grouped or solo.  I still taunt when soloing (dam habits) but i also keep myself buffed and healed.  Adds = death if I cannot root park all and then camp hehe.<br />
<br />
And in groups, another viable crowd controller is the bard.<br />
<br />
Why do I solo?  Xp is generally better, I only die to my own stupidity, and I win all roles.<br />
<br />
Why do i group, fighting is non-stop, I rarely die unless someone is stupid, and it is not as boring.						</td>
					</tr>
															</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=3489">Naval</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">3/15/2002 - 12:59 AM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=3212">Naval</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														I'd say soloing can be fun (some nice long range arrows), but most zones make its a bit hard, sure i could solo the spiders etc. in DL, but once i got a few adds and they decided to root me..., DL is a definate must have group zone or be killing at a lvl when everything is lb.<br />
<br />
OT on the otherhad has say one oger that is great exp when soloed, at 39 gives about half a blue of exp per 6 min spawn and occasionally good loot, 6mins is just about right for the down time and its a nice camp.<br />
<br />
Basically i would say area has allot to do with it more than class.<br />
<br />
Of course i find i can get into most groups due to sow/snare and have found many groups allready wanting to fear kite in DL which thoes two spells make viable.<br />
<br />
I would say few people will refuse to have a ranger in their group as they have melle which is as good as a warrior (without critics) and have some nice utility spells.<br />
<br />
The only problem i find in getting a group is when they seek a tank and do not intent to fear kite, i know i can hold some mobs, but not the ones lvl 50's want to be killing (being that i lvl 40) without some serios healing (double attacking for 107 a hit becomes scary with only 1100 hp ish unbuffed).						</td>
					</tr>
